// Temporal half of the transfer_to_team rule: at most once per session, matching
// src/outbound_ivr/voice/agent.py's `state.transfer_to_team_requested` guard ("Only call
// this once per call. If you already called it once, do not call it again."). Pairs
// with the plain permit in policies/dogwood/transfer_to_team.dw -- forbid always wins
// over permit, so the two compose into "allowed once per session, with a non-empty
// reason and case_id".
//
// Shape follows "Cap how many times an action runs",
// https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/
// example-policies-temporal.html#example-policies-temporal-rate-limit: `count` counts
// matching events in the window, including the request being authorized, so the
// second call in the window is the first to be denied (`n > 1`). The window is 24
// hours, the documented maximum for a temporal condition (and the maximum trajectory
// look-back a session keeps) -- there is no "for the rest of the session, however
// long" window; 24h is as close as Dogwood's syntax gets, and matches
// "Securing AI agents with temporal policies in Amazon Bedrock AgentCore"
// (https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/securing-ai-agents-with-temporal-policies-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/):
// "agent trajectories carry a maximum look-back window of 24 hours."
//
// Per-session caps are a behavior-shaping control, not a security boundary: the
// caller supplies the session ID, so a caller who controls it could reset the count by
// starting a new session (same caveat the AWS doc gives for its own rate-limit
// example). outbound_ivr.tools.business and src/outbound_ivr/voice/agent.py do not independently
// re-check this across a session restart either, so this is a documented, matched gap,
// not a new one.
forbid(
  principal,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"OutboundIvrTools___transfer_to_team",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"${GATEWAY_ARN}"
) when temporal {
  exists (n: Long).
    (count for (t: Timepoint).
      where (formerly within 24h (AgentCore::Action::"OutboundIvrTools___transfer_to_team"::request{ eventResource: resource } && tp(t)))) == n
    && n > 1
};
